Key Claim: A organization is recognized as a legal entity (pháp nhân) in Vietnam when it fulfills the following criteria:

a) Established according to the provisions of the Civil Code or other relevant laws;

b) Has an organizational structure as prescribed by Article 83 of the Civil Code;

c) Possesses independent assets separate from those of individuals and other legal entities, and is responsible for its liabilities with its own assets;

d) Acts in legal relations in its own name.

